# Ticket geometry

- Every new or modified ticket-style control or card needs a clearly visible inward circular scoop at each of its four outer corners. Use the approved hamburger tickets as the minimum visual reference: their corner scoop is 10 CSS pixels on a roughly 60–80px-tall ticket. Scale the scoop up on larger tickets so it stays equally pronounced, never smaller or barely visible. Where the approved ticket pattern uses them, retain the inward semicircular scoops at the centers of both side edges too.
- The corner cutouts are concave: they remove part of the ticket body and reveal the background. A rounded outer corner, 45-degree chamfer, or colored circle drawn over the ticket is not equivalent.
- Preserve existing live values, labels, links, actions, and data sources when correcting ticket shape.
- Verify all four corners and both side scoops at the intended desktop and mobile viewports. Check that no cutout clips text, artwork, or focus treatment.
- On mobile, preserve the intended layout instead of making tickets taller or forcing everything into one column. The My Activity filters are two tickets, two tickets, then a full-width Completed ticket even on a narrow phone. Compact two-column tickets may be about 2:1 width-to-height if their icon, label, count, and scoops remain legible and unclipped. Scale internal padding, type, icons, and scoops together; keep the full-width odd ticket about the same height as its neighbors. Check the narrowest supported phone width and the breakpoint just before stacking.
- Use the ticket fill and concave mask to define the edge. Do not add a persistent white, blue, or other outline around the full perimeter just to show selection; keep a visible focus treatment only for keyboard focus.
- A responsive ticket change must retain the original link/button target, keyboard focus, and full clickable area; CSS geometry is not permission to remove or replace an interaction.
- Visual references: the approved hamburger ticket shape and the owner's close-up of its pronounced corner scoop, September 25, 2026. The My Activity yellow-circle screenshot identifies every corner requiring this shape.
